description:
Implement the reverse-lookup matcher that, given an embedded content vector, ranks Analysis Categories and the user's existing Projects, and decides match-vs-create. Part of epic ao-gpx.

DEPENDENCIES: embedding client (ao-8fy), schema/helpers (ao-7hw), taxonomy seed (ao-i6q).

NEW FILE: packages/db/src/classify.ts (export from src/index.ts). Pure decision logic over embeddings — no Gemini calls here; the embedding vector is passed in.

API:
- export interface CategoryMatch { path: string; name: string; purpose: string; score: number }
- export interface ProjectMatch { projectId: string; score: number }
- export async function classifyContent(args: {
    ownerId: string;
    contentEmbedding: number[];        // already prefixed+embedded by the worker
    projectMatchMin: number;           // env CLASSIFY_PROJECT_MATCH_MIN (0.82)
    categoryMatchMin: number;          // env CLASSIFY_CATEGORY_MATCH_MIN (0.75)
    topK?: number;                     // default 5
  }): Promise<{
    categories: CategoryMatch[];       // top-K above categoryMatchMin, desc by score
    bestProject: ProjectMatch | null;  // top project if >= projectMatchMin, else null
  }>
  IMPLEMENTATION (v1, brute force in-memory — fine for tens of categories + a handful of user projects; pgvector is a deferred follow-up):
    - load listCategoryEmbeddings() and listProjectEmbeddings(ownerId)
    - cosineSimilarity(contentEmbedding, row.embedding) for each
    - filter/sort; return.

NOTE: cosineSimilarity lives in apps/worker/src/lib/embeddings.ts but classify.ts is in packages/db. To avoid a db->worker dependency, put a small cosineSimilarity in packages/db (or a shared util). Decide and document: simplest is to inline a private cosine in classify.ts (a few lines), keeping packages/db dependency-free.

ACCEPTANCE: given hand-built vectors, classifyContent returns expected ranking and respects thresholds (covered by smoke bead). bun check-types + bun lint pass.
